	(text "1. Bare 1.5 mm ENIG pads on the bottom side, without paste or a fitted part; they are not in the BOM.\n2. All pads sit on the 2.54 mm grid of the host header PI1, so one pogo-pin plate reaches all 28 pads.\n3. Pos counts along the row from its silkscreen label (west to east in top view).\n4. Each row has its own GND pad: TP6 and TP40 here; TP24, TP25, TP26 and TP47 are drawn on sheet 11 (Local probe ground returns).\n5. A bench supply goes into TP1 (+) and TP6 (GND), never into TP39, and never with a powered host fitted.\n6. Programming and test fixtures keep the actuator permits inactive."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 222.25 208.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a4344fe4-f01e-5f0f-a017-419ac6c08a98")
	)
